{"term":"dive","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ae0c1d2a006d697a0f","definition":"To swim under water.","example":"He dove in the water to save her.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c17ab4a91a171f1f9f","definition":"To jump into water head-first.","example":"It is not that pearls fetch a high price because men have dived for them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e847e974e1f35a20a3","definition":"To jump headfirst toward the ground or into another substance.","example":"to dive into home plate","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68ca378eacc1afccdf","definition":"To descend sharply or steeply.","example":"[the Hammersmith & City at Paddington]: There it dived underground, eventually enabling its train services to run over, and be entangled with, the easterly extensions of the Metropolitan and the District.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9817a2c8c5f32e72ea","definition":"To lose altitude quickly by pointing downwards, as with a bird or aircraft.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:929a353d25b7c5679f","definition":"To undertake with enthusiasm.","example":"She dove right in and started making improvements.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"especially","register":"especially, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c66183ecb3f313d779","definition":"To deliberately fall down after a challenge, imitating being fouled, in the hope of getting one's opponent penalised.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cef961c8ffd8eb93a8","definition":"To leap while fielding to take a brilliant catch which usually results in a wicket and appreciation.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4ae296b29e42550859","definition":"To cause to descend, dunk; to plunge something into water.","example":"To dive an infant either thrice or but once in Baptism","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary v